-- The venues a reward can be redeemed at.
--
-- Generated by hand and reviewed by hand, like `0013_sour_apocalypse.sql`
-- through `0020_pos_terminals_business.sql`.
--
-- ## What this closes
--
-- A reward has never had a venue. `rewards` carries the business, the cost, the
-- stock and the auto-grant threshold, so "this reward is available at Sucursal
-- Centro" could not be expressed and `RewardAvailableAtBranch` (the trigger in
-- `docs/19-Geolocalizacion-Notificaciones.md` §7.4) had nothing to read.
--
-- **A join table, not a column.** A business with three venues will scope a
-- reward to two of them; a nullable `rewards.branch_id` forces a choice of one
-- and changing it later is a data migration.
--
-- **No rows means every venue.** That is what a reward meant before this table
-- existed, so this migration inserts nothing and no existing reward changes
-- meaning. There is no backfill to get wrong.
--
-- ## Why `business_id` is duplicated
--
-- The RLS policy is `business_id = current_setting(...)`. Reading it through a
-- join to `rewards` would put a join inside every policy evaluation and give
-- tenancy a second place to be wrong. The column is not free — an insert can
-- carry a `business_id` that disagrees with its reward's — which is why the
-- reward API validates the venue ids against the caller's own `branches` before
-- writing, and why the API, not the table, is the boundary that must be right.
--
-- ## Deletion
--
-- Both foreign keys cascade. Deleting a venue removes it from every reward's
-- scope, which is the only sensible reading: the reward stays, available at the
-- venues that remain. Deleting a reward removes its scope with it.
--
-- Applied in production by hand. A plain `CREATE TABLE` on a new table takes no
-- lock on anything that exists, so no `CONCURRENTLY` is needed here; the index
-- is built against a table that is empty at creation time.
CREATE TABLE "reward_branches" (
	"reward_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"branch_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"business_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"created_at" timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
	CONSTRAINT "reward_branches_pkey" PRIMARY KEY("reward_id","branch_id")
);
--> statement-breakpoint
